  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Inga laurina",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inga_laurina",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1329657381,
      "text": "Inga laurina is a species of plant in the family Fabaceae. It native to an area from Mexico south to Argentina, including in the Caribbean. The species is present throughout most of Brazil, where it is called ingá-mirim due to the relatively small pods."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Inga laurina",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inga_laurina",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 226097118,
      "text": "Inga laurina, l’Arbre à miel, Pois doux ou Pois doux blanc, est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Fabaceae. Son aire d'origine s'étend de l'ouest et du sud du Mexique à l'Amérique tropicale. C'est un arbre qui pousse principalement dans le biome tropical humide. Il est utilisé comme médicament et comme nourriture pour les invertébrés, il a des utilisations environnementales et sert de combustible et de nourriture."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Inga laurina",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inga_laurina",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 70206031,
      "text": "Inga laurina é uma árvore da família Fabaceae nativa do Brasil, não endêmica conhecida pelos nomes populares: ingá-mirim, ingá-feijão, ingá-lagarta, ingá-pequeno, ingá-branco, ingá-da-praia, ingá-chichi, ingá-chichica, ingá-cururu, ingaí.\nA espécie foi descrita pelo botânico Carl Ludwig von Willdenow no ano de 1806."
    }
